WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.709 --> 00:00:08.130
Long ago, a wealthy landowner lived in Louisiana.

2
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.671
His name was Charles Durance.

3
00:00:12.151 --> 00:00:14.392
He had two daughters who were getting married.

4
00:00:15.092 --> 00:00:18.633
Their weddings were planned for the same day at their father's farm.

5
00:00:19.393 --> 00:00:22.214
Mr. Durance loved his daughters very much.

6
00:00:23.094 --> 00:00:26.075
So, he decided to prepare a big surprise for them.

7
00:00:26.095 --> 00:00:30.296
"My daughters' weddings are coming up.

8
00:00:30.948 --> 00:00:33.209
Is there a way to make it a special day for them?"

9
00:00:33.529 --> 00:00:34.089
he wondered.

10
00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:38.510
After days of thinking, he came up with a wonderful idea.

11
00:00:42.371 --> 00:00:43.992
He went to talk to his servants.

12
00:00:44.012 --> 00:00:46.212
"I need lots of spiders.

13
00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:47.493
Where can I get some?"

14
00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:48.553
he asked.

15
00:00:48.573 --> 00:00:53.074
"You can probably get them from China," one of his servants replied.

16
00:00:53.094 --> 00:00:55.395
"How many spiders do you need?"

17
00:00:55.415 --> 00:00:58.076
"I need millions of them," said Mr.

18
00:01:00.364 --> 00:01:02.045
Durance. The servants were surprised.

19
00:01:02.846 --> 00:01:04.267
"Spiders are expensive.

20
00:01:04.747 --> 00:01:08.630
They will have to come on a ship from China," one servant explained.

21
00:01:09.311 --> 00:01:11.252
Charles ordered the spiders anyway.

22
00:01:11.893 --> 00:01:15.616
Several months later, a shipload of spiders arrived from China.

23
00:01:16.236 --> 00:01:19.859
"What shall we do with all the spiders?"

24
00:01:20.319 --> 00:01:21.520
the servants asked Mr.

25
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.504
Durance. "Let them loose in the trees along the road to the house," he instructed.

26
00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:31.394
"Why are we letting all of these spiders loose?"

27
00:01:31.754 --> 00:01:32.275
they wondered.

28
00:01:32.295 --> 00:01:35.358
"It's almost time for his daughters' weddings."

29
00:01:35.838 --> 00:01:37.880
Mr. Durance's servants were puzzled.

30
00:01:41.263 --> 00:01:45.387
Over the next few days, the spiders spun webs throughout the trees.

31
00:01:45.967 --> 00:01:47.809
Mr. Durance called his servants.

32
00:01:48.469 --> 00:01:49.931
"I want you to go into town.

33
00:01:50.411 --> 00:01:55.836
Order two hundred kilograms each of gold and silver powder from California," he directed.

34
00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:04.822
"Did he just tell us to order two hundred kilograms each of gold and silver powder?"

35
00:02:05.282 --> 00:02:06.142
they asked each other.

36
00:02:06.162 --> 00:02:07.742
"That's what he said.

37
00:02:08.243 --> 00:02:10.543
He certainly has the money to buy the powder.

38
00:02:11.383 --> 00:02:12.804
But why does he need it?"

39
00:02:13.304 --> 00:02:15.585
The servants were puzzled and curious.

40
00:02:16.465 --> 00:02:19.646
A few days later, the gold and silver powder arrived.

41
00:02:20.246 --> 00:02:22.546
Charles Durance was very satisfied.

42
00:02:23.207 --> 00:02:25.427
It was the day of his two daughters' weddings.

43
00:02:25.447 --> 00:02:28.108
"Sprinkle the powder on the spider webs!"

44
00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:28.961
he ordered.

45
00:02:30.822 --> 00:02:33.824
Mr. Durance's instructions surprised the servants again.

46
00:02:34.525 --> 00:02:37.888
But they did as he said and sprinkled the powder on the webs.

47
00:02:38.808 --> 00:02:42.351
When they were finished, they saw what Charles Durance had planned.

48
00:02:44.233 --> 00:02:47.415
The spider webs along the road sparkled in the sunlight.

49
00:02:47.435 --> 00:02:48.997
"Look at this!"

50
00:02:49.557 --> 00:02:50.538
the guests marveled.

51
00:02:50.558 --> 00:02:53.781
"Oh my, this is beautiful!"

52
00:02:54.121 --> 00:02:54.922
they exclaimed.

53
00:02:55.742 --> 00:03:00.338
The beautiful, sparkling spider webs amazed everyone who came to the weddings.

54
00:03:00.358 --> 00:03:03.620
"Haven't I planned a beautiful wedding day for you?"

55
00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.941
Mr. Durance remarked to his daughters.

56
00:03:05.961 --> 00:03:10.424
"Father, thank you so much!

57
00:03:10.965 --> 00:03:12.326
It is so beautiful!"

58
00:03:13.006 --> 00:03:14.267
they replied with delight.

59
00:03:14.287 --> 00:03:21.372
"Well," their father explained, "I wanted you both to have the most expensive weddings in the world!"
